scenario a receiver that stops asserting does not recover by the clock
describe Trace 05 is the same rule over three epochs; this one runs it past the
describe evidence TTL, which is where the rule used to stop holding.
describe
describe The receiver alarms, then reports `unknown` about spoofing for the rest
describe of the session — the LS550G's state per OWNER_DECISIONS OD-5 section 2,
describe not a hypothetical part. `unknown` is left alone rather than cleared, so
describe the alarm stays live until the TTL takes it out of the score at 15 s.
describe
describe Every fix here is a good one, so validity never leaves `valid` and no
describe other reason weighs anything: from 15 s the score is a genuine zero.
describe That zero used to start the clean hold, and the device walked back up
describe through Degraded to Trusted by 26 s with no all-clear anywhere in the
describe trace. The steps at 21 s and 26 s are what that looked like.
describe
describe Recovery arrives when the receiver says so and not before, and the hold
describe is measured from the all-clear rather than from the silence in front of
describe it — which is what the last three steps pin.

at 0
  fix 3d
  pos 5000000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  sats 11 14
  jam none
  spoof critical
  expect trust untrusted
  expect reason receiver-spoofing
  expect validity valid              # the fix is still a fix; it is not trusted

# The receiver stops saying anything about spoofing. The alarm stands.
at 5000
  fix 3d
  pos 5000010 10000010
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  sats 11 14
  jam none
  spoof unknown
  expect trust untrusted
  expect reason receiver-spoofing

# One second before the TTL, and it is still counted.
at 14000
  fix 3d
  pos 5000020 10000020
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  sats 11 14
  jam none
  spoof unknown
  expect trust untrusted
  expect reason receiver-spoofing

# And past it. The allegation stops counting towards the score — and does not
# thereby become an all-clear.
at 16000
  fix 3d
  pos 5000030 10000030
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  sats 11 14
  jam none
  spoof unknown
  expect no-reason receiver-spoofing
  expect validity valid
  expect trust untrusted

at 21000
  fix 3d
  pos 5000040 10000040
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  sats 11 14
  jam none
  spoof unknown
  expect trust untrusted            # the old code showed Degraded here

at 26000
  fix 3d
  pos 5000050 10000050
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  sats 11 14
  jam none
  spoof unknown
  expect trust untrusted            # ...and Trusted here

# The receiver says it positively. Recovery starts now, not thirty seconds ago.
at 30000
  fix 3d
  pos 5000060 10000060
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  sats 11 14
  jam none
  spoof none
  expect trust untrusted

at 35000
  fix 3d
  pos 5000070 10000070
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  sats 12 15
  jam none
  spoof none
  expect trust degraded

at 40000
  fix 3d
  pos 5000080 10000080
  alt 42000
  acc 3400
  sats 12 15
  jam none
  spoof none
  expect trust trusted
